<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Cooked Finance"
  description="Cooked Finance privacy policy. Your financial inputs never leave your browser. Learn what data we do and don't collect, how cookies and ads work, and your rights."
  path="/privacy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lead="The short version: your financial numbers stay on your device. We can't see them."
  updated="June 5, 2026"
>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Cooked Finance ("we", "us", or "our")
    handles information when you visit <strong>cookedfinance.com</strong> (the
    "Site"). We've designed the Site to be privacy-friendly by default.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you enter</h2>
  <p>
    The financial details you type into the calculator — your age, annual income,
    savings, and debt — are processed <strong>entirely within your browser</strong>.
    This information is never sent to our servers, never stored in a database, and
    never shared with third parties. Your most recent result may be saved locally
    on your own device using your browser's <code>localStorage</code> so you can
    see it again later; you can clear it at any time by clearing your browser data.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>
    Like most websites, we may collect limited, non-identifying technical
    information through standard analytics and server logs, such as:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Browser type and device category</li>
    <li>Approximate region (derived from IP, not stored alongside your inputs)</li>
    <li>Pages visited and referring site</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This data is aggregate and used only to understand traffic and improve the
    Site. It is not linked to the financial values you enter.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    We may use cookies and similar technologies for basic functionality and
    analytics. We may also display advertising, including through Google AdSense.
    Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on prior
    visits to this and other websites. You can opt out of personalized advertising
    by visiting
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>,
    and learn more at
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google's advertising policies</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
    personal information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clear your browser storage to remove any saved result.</li>
    <li>Use your browser settings to block or delete cookies.</li>
    <li>Opt out of personalized ads via the links above.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on
    this page with an updated date above.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy? Reach us through our
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
